  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "lapsed_date": "18/04/2024",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (01 Rev A, 01, 02, 03 & 04, received on 30/03/2021) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with this approval and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied and thereafter retained as such.",
    "Condition : 4 - The use of the property as a residential care home hereby approved shall not commence until space has been laid out within the site in accordance with approved plan no. 01 Rev A for at least two bicycles to be parked and that space shall thereafter be kept available for the parking of bicycles.",
    "Condition : 5 - Before the use of the property as a residential care home is brought into use, a visibility splay of 2.4 metres x 2.4 metres shall be provided on each side of the vehicular access (the depth measured from the back of the footway and the widths outwards from the edges of the access). Thereafter, no fence, wall or other obstruction to visibility exceeding 0.6 metres in height above the surface of the adjoining highway shall be erected, planted or allowed to grow within the areas of such splays.",
    "Condition : 6 - Before the use of the property as a residential care home is brought into use, the redundant section of vehicular access to 1 Bulstrode Road shall be permanently closed and full-height kerbs and footway reinstated so that it cannot be used as an access across the pavement.",
    "Condition : 7 - Before the use of the property as a residential care home is brought into use, a wall no greater than 0.6 metres in height shall be erected on each side of the car parking space and retained thereafter. The boundary treatment shall be completed before the use hereby approved commences and two pedestrian gates providing access the front entrance and bike and bin stores shall be installed.",
    "Condition : 8 - The premises shall be used for a residential care home and shall not be used for purposes other than those within Class C2 (residential institution) and for no other purpose (including any other purpose within the Schedule to the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987, or in any provision equivalent to that Class in any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification)."
  ],
